## Git Command Execution Rules

### Safe Commands (Auto-Execute)
- `git status`
- `git log`
- `git diff`
- `git branch -l`
- `git show`
- `git blame`

### Confirmation Required
- `git commit`
- `git push`
- `git checkout`
- `git merge`
- `git rebase`
- `git pull`
- `git stash`

### Explicit Permission Required
- `git push --force`
- `git reset --hard`
- `git clean -fd`
- `git rebase -i`
- `git cherry-pick`
- Operations on protected branches (main/develop)

### Prohibited Without User Override
- Force push to main/develop
- Delete remote branches
- Modify published history
- Commit to protected branches directly

